blocks.text:
### A node: an element plus a link

Stacks, queues and linked lists can all be built as a **linked sequence of nodes**. A **node** stores two things:

- the **element**: the value stored in the node;
- the **link**: which node comes next in the sequence.

In C a node is a struct (Day 13), and the link is a **pointer** to the next node:

```c
struct node {
    int elem;
    struct node *next;
};
```

A struct may contain a pointer to its own type. It may **not** contain a whole member of its own type: a node that contains a node that contains a node... would be infinitely big. gcc refuses:

