Using a local node:

```c
struct node n;     // WRONG: automatic storage
n.elem = elem;
n.next = s->top;
s->top = &n;
```

This compiles, but `n` dies when `push` returns, so `top` is left as a **dangling pointer** (Day 12). Using it later is undefined behaviour. Nodes must come from `malloc`.

